  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Whenever someone logs in or logs out, the social menu online friends list is immediately refreshed and sorted. This results in all thumbnails jumping around, as in this video: https://www.dropbox.com/s/9zxl28qyughvgg9/2020-10-17%2009-08-59.mp4?dl=0\nIn particular, when expanding online friends, thumbnails can jump between the leftmost and rightmost sides of the online friends list, making it very difficult to select them.\nI would suggest some combination of the following to help address this:\n* When users go offline with the social menu open, make their thumbnail show the offline status (as in the favorites row) but leave the thumbnail where it is until the menu is closed\n* When users on favorites lists go online, keep them in the same position (or put them at the end of the online users part of the favorites section in question) until the social menu is closed\n* When users on the overall online friends list go online, put them on the rightmost end of the list (top to bottom), regardless of where they would normally be placed, and sort only when the menu is closed. Keep the current scroll position unchanged.\nThis will allow players to still see when friends go online or offline immediately, but will avoid moving thumbnails you might be trying to select.",
